 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Konjunktiv I: forms",
     "texto": [
      "It is formed with the verb stem plus the endings **-e, -est, -e, -en, -et, -en**: **er komme** (he says he is coming), **sie habe** (she says she has). Only the singular and the third person are common. The verb **sein** is the most important: **ich sei, du seiest, er sei, wir seien, ihr seiet, sie seien**.",
      "With **haben** and **werden** too: **er habe**, **er werde**. The other verbs are formed in the same way."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Indirect style",
     "texto": [
      "It is used to present other people's words: **Er sagt, er sei krank** / **Er sagt, dass er krank sei**. Without **dass**, the conjugated verb usually occupies the second position; with **dass**, it goes at the end. Konjunktiv I marks reported speech, not time: this is understood from the verb form and the context. It does not imply that the reporter doubts what was said."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
